From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer: recompute freeform task bounds each frame

content_frames survives across setup_set calls. Unioning new layers into
the previous frame's bounds retains maximized sizes and old task positions,
and even restores those stale sizes when a task window is recreated.
Clear the map before collecting the current frame's layers so only layers
in the same frame contribute to a task's bounds.

Original work for waydroid-nvidia; modifies Apache-2.0 hwcomposer sources.
---
 hwcomposer/modes/multi-window.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/hwcomposer/modes/multi-window.cpp b/hwcomposer/modes/multi-window.cpp
--- a/hwcomposer/modes/multi-window.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/modes/multi-window.cpp
@@ -71,5 +71,6 @@ int multi_window_mode::prepare(hwc_layer_1* hwc_layer, size_t) {
 int multi_window_mode::setup_set(waydroid_hwc_composer_device_1* pdev, hwc_display_contents_1_t* contents) {
     layer_infos.setup(pdev, contents->hwLayers, contents->numHwLayers);
+    content_frames.clear();
     if (pdev->display->resizeFollowsWindow && !pdev->display->resizeUsesReconnect)
         display_resize_arm(pdev->display, 0, 0); // clear an earlier single-window override
     if (pdev->display->wantDecorations) {
